# SHA-256 of each domain a real deployment uses, and of the owner's personal
# addresses at public mail providers. A hostname under one of these domains,
# or one of these addresses, fails scripts/wrangler-config.test.mjs even when
# public-hosts.txt allows the host (decision D-16). The hash keeps the names
# out of the public tree. It is no secret: a short domain is easy to guess
# from its hash.
# Add one with: printf %s <domain or address, lower case> | shasum -a 256
